Z||000029||pontiacs4me||08-06-2001||02:43 AM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR>[B]Ok I have weighed up the half door skin as apposed to a replacement for the lower aero ground effects trims on the doors and guards. The half doorskins are going to actually be harder to fit, and manufacture without having a risk of screwing up tolerances, than just making a part that goes along the bottom of your original doors and will mould in easily. <P><BR>I have read this paragraph over and over, and for some reason I cannot understand what the message is about.  Could someone please help me out here.  Maybe its just too late.  <BR>Hey aus, you are the man.  Im putting in an order, but it will be awhile, Im getting ready to start back to school in 2 weeks $$$$$.  I was wondering one thing, are these made of the original type plastic, or are these fiberglass?  thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000030||AusFiero||08-06-2001||03:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pontiacs4me:<BR><B>[QUOTE]Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR>[B]Ok I have weighed up the half door skin as apposed to a replacement for the lower aero ground effects trims on the doors and guards. The half doorskins are going to actually be harder to fit, and manufacture without having a risk of screwing up tolerances, than just making a part that goes along the bottom of your original doors and will mould in easily. <P><BR>I have read this paragraph over and over, and for some reason I cannot understand what the message is about.  Could someone please help me out here.  Maybe its just too late.  <BR>Hey aus, you are the man.  Im putting in an order, but it will be awhile, Im getting ready to start back to school in 2 weeks $$$$$.  I was wondering one thing, are these made of the original type plastic, or are these fiberglass?  thanks.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>All will be better explained in the next couple of hours in a new thread. But the price is going to drop by a fair bit also.<P>On the door skins versus the original design. I have discovered too many things that could go wrong by using half skins. Now it will just be a case of removing your lower GT aero trims on the door and front guard and replacing them with new pieces and moulding the upper edge in with a very small amount of filler (about 1/32" in thickness) after using blind rivets and glue, or just glue if you get the right glue. I thought the other way would be easier but it isn't. I experimented today and in fact it was down right hard using the half door skin idea whne I tried to sticka piece of fiberglass to it. Mind you I have to get a new doorskin for my car now because I cut 1 in half  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Luckily Dave at Ponti-World has 1.<P>On the glue on piece we have a product in Australia called Araldite KP36 which sticks fibreglass to anything, metal, plastic, even concrete and is sandalbe just like car body filler. Does anybody know if you have a product the same in the USA that I could recommend people use?<P>I am also renting a workshop tomorrow so I get no distractions to get this job done faster. At $62 a week for a workshop the size of a 6 car garage it was hard to knock back. Taking it short term at first but the way demand for stuff is going I may take out a full time lease on it for development purposes and to store the other Fiero I am after. My wife will  be glad to have her garage spot back. Plus I am aiming now to have all of stage 2 finished in 1 month. <P>Anyway will post the new cheaper prices and more explanetory pictures later in another thread, as said. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000031||MinnGreenGT||08-06-2001||10:39 AM||||AUS-<P>I Love it!  I spent a little time in PhotoShop this weekend, but accidentally saved over my high-res copy- so I'm starting over again.  Anyway, just figured I'd post what I had to bump the topic a little!  I'll be placing an order sometime soon... when my wife says that I've got enough money in the bank.  Are you possibly going to offer a package special with both the side scoops and lower skirts/sills/whatever?<P>Thanks!<BR>Rob Bartlett<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/custgreengt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
